(15,'2026-06-24 20:59:13','Identify','legislative capital	The legislative capital of South Africa is Cape Town. While Pretoria serves as the administrative capital, with its Union Buildings serving as a symbol of government offices and decision-making, it is Cape Town that holds the title for legislative purposes in the country. The city hosts several important legislative bodies, including the Parliament of South Africa which is responsible for making laws (legislative) and government operations within the National Assembly. Therefore, based on this data, Cape Town is indeed recognized as the legislative capital of South Africa.','INVALID','my-model'),
